 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nShape height property adds unexpected offset\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen setting the height property on inline shapes, an unexpected offset of 1 is being added to the cy value. This causes shapes to be rendered with incorrect dimensions.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.shared import Inches\n\n# Create a document and add an image\ndoc = Document()\nparagraph = doc.paragraphs[0]\nrun = paragraph.runs[0] if paragraph.runs else paragraph.add_run()\n\n# Add an inline shape (image)\ninline_shape = run.add_picture('image.png', width=Inches(2), height=Inches(3))\n\n# The height should be exactly what we set\nexpected_height = Inches(3)\nactual_height = inline_shape.height\n\nprint(f\"Expected height: {expected_height}\")\nprint(f\"Actual height: {actual_height}\")\n# Shows that actual height is 1 unit more than expected\n```\n\nThe issue also affects the underlying XML structure where the cy attribute gets an extra +1 added to its value, causing rendering inconsistencies.\n</issue>\n",
